<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Jonathan Zalzman Guitar"
  description="A local-business website for a guitar teacher and working musician, designed to turn 'maybe I'll learn guitar' into a booked free trial lesson."
  client="Jonathan Zalzman (Suwanee, Georgia, US)"
  role="Design & development"
  year="2026"
  liveUrl="https://jonathanzalzmanguitar.netlify.app"
  slides={[
    {
      title: 'Hero and teaching styles',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-jonathan-zalzman-intro.mp4',
      poster: '/images/jonathan-zalzman-intro.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Pricing and reviews',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-jonathan-zalzman-pricing.mp4',
      poster: '/images/jonathan-zalzman-pricing.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Booking form',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-jonathan-zalzman-booking.mp4',
      poster: '/images/jonathan-zalzman-booking.webp',
    },
  ]}
  highlights={[
    { value: 'Hand-coded', label: 'No page builder, no plugins, fast first paint on a phone' },
    { value: '9 style pages', label: 'One specific pitch per style instead of a generic lesson list' },
    { value: 'One path to book', label: 'Every CTA leads to the trial-lesson form, phone or email' },
  ]}
  overview={[
    'Jonathan teaches guitar, bass and ukulele in Suwanee, Georgia and online, and he still gigs. That second part is the whole positioning: <strong>"Learn guitar from a working musician."</strong> The site had to make that credibility obvious in one glance and then remove every excuse not to book.',
    'The design leans into performance photography on a dark background, so it looks like a musician\'s site rather than a tutoring directory. Nine teaching styles (rock and blues, funk, jazz and fusion, prog and shred, metal, theory and ear training, bass and ukulele, songwriting, improvisation) each get a short, specific pitch instead of a generic "all levels welcome". Three five-star reviews from students of different ages sit right where a parent or an adult beginner would start to hesitate.',
    'Pricing is completely in the open: the first lesson is free, then 30 or 60 minute lessons at a flat rate, with no registration fee, contract or subscription. Putting the numbers on the page filters out tire-kickers and makes the booking form feel low-risk. The form itself collects just enough (instrument, experience, in-person or online) and every call to action on the page leads back to it, alongside tap-to-call and email links.',
    'The site is hand-coded HTML, CSS and JavaScript on Netlify: no page builder, no plugins to update, and nothing between the visitor and a fast first paint on a phone.',
  ]}
  tools={['HTML & CSS', 'JavaScript', 'Netlify', 'Netlify Forms', 'Figma', 'Photoshop']}
/>
